## 7. Residual Risk Assessment

### 7.1 Risks Addressed by Automation

| Risk                                                | Before Automation | After Automation | Reduction |
| --------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- | ---------------- | --------- |
| Lost or stolen asset remains undetected             | High              | Low              | 75%       |
| Unauthorized asset movement outside designated zone | High              | Low              | 75%       |
| Delayed SOC notification                            | High              | Low              | 80%       |
| Delayed incident response                           | High              | Medium           | 50%       |
| Lack of auditable asset-location evidence           | Medium            | Low              | 70%       |



### 7.2 Residual Risks

| Risk                              | Description                                                                                                                 | Mitigation                                                                                                                                                 | Acceptance |
| --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- |
| Loss of telemetry                 | A laptop may lose network connectivity, power, or monitoring-agent functionality and therefore stop reporting its location. | Monitor agent health and last-seen timestamps; generate an exception when expected telemetry is absent.                                                    | Required   |
| Geolocation inaccuracy            | Location data may be inaccurate or insufficient to determine whether an asset has crossed a control-zone boundary.          | Use defined geofence tolerances and require employee/Security Administrator verification before escalation or remediation.                                 | Required   |
| Employee confirmation unavailable | An employee may be unreachable or unable to confirm whether the asset is secured.                                           | Escalate the event to the SOC and Security Administrator rather than treating lack of confirmation as automatic authorization for destructive remediation. | Required   |
| Unauthorized remote wipe decision | A remote wipe could destroy evidence or disrupt legitimate recovery efforts if performed incorrectly.                       | Maintain `auto_remediate: False`; require Security Administrator review and management authorization.                                                      | Required   |



### 7.3 Automation-Introduced Risks

| Risk                | Description                                                                                                                                                                        | Mitigation                                                                                                                                                          |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Automation failure  | Failure of OpenNinja, the endpoint agent, communications path, geofence engine, or alerting pipeline could prevent a breach from being detected or reported.                       | Monitor system health and telemetry freshness; maintain logging and alerting for failed monitoring components; establish manual verification procedures.            |
| False positives     | Legitimate asset movement may be incorrectly interpreted as a zone breach because of geolocation inaccuracies, temporary connectivity issues, or incorrect geofence configuration. | Require employee verification and Security Administrator review before incident escalation or remote wipe.                                                          |
| False negatives     | An asset could leave an authorized zone without generating an alert because telemetry is unavailable or the geofence is incorrectly configured.                                    | Monitor last-seen status, validate geofence configuration, periodically test RULE-003, and maintain manual asset-accountability procedures.                         |
| Privacy exposure    | Continuous location monitoring creates information about employee and asset movement that may exceed the minimum information required for security purposes.                       | Limit collection to the security objective, restrict access to authorized personnel, establish retention requirements, and obtain appropriate privacy/legal review. |
| Configuration error | Incorrect zones, asset assignments, alert thresholds, or rule configuration could produce inaccurate compliance results.                                                           | Implement configuration change control, administrative review, testing, and periodic validation of geofences and RULE-003 parameters.                               |




